<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Othmar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 689–759</span> · Also known as Otmar of Saint Gall</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Othmar was an Alemannic priest who in 719 founded the Abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a> at the site of the hermit Gallus's cell and became its first abbot. He introduced the Benedictine rule and founded a hospital and a home for lepers. In a dispute with Frankish counts over the abbey's lands he was imprisoned and died in exile on the island of Werd in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 759.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-othmar.jpg" alt="Saint Othmar" width="300" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Otmar_von_St-Gallen2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
